I commented on and closed the two issues this session fixed. I skipped the other six because I did no work on them.

#963 (flaky compact-thrash tests): closed. Fixed in commit 0f9d50ab.
• **Change:** the counter logic now takes the counter as a parameter, and each of the four tests that used to write the shared global counter now uses its own private copy. Nothing in these tests is shared anymore. I also removed the four matching entries from the known-race list.
• **Verification:** the two flaky tests passed 20 of 20 repeated runs, and the full cargo test passed. That's evidence the race is gone, not proof.

#964 (silent `max_tokens` warning): closed. Fixed in commit 66edf3b3. There were two bugs, and fixing only the first would have caused a false alarm:
• **Silent:** quiet mode muted the warning, and quiet mode switches on automatically for CI and piped runs, which is exactly where the failure happened. The warning now prints in quiet mode too.
• **Wrong limit:** on Anthropic it compared against the preset's default of 64000 rather than the model's real maximum of 128000. So with only the first fix, the legal value 128000 would have triggered a warning. For claude-opus-5* models it now uses 128000.
• **Tests:** 131072 now warns, 128000 stays quiet, and the existing DeepSeek cases still pass.
• **Still open:** only the `claude-opus-5*` models have a known maximum. For any other Anthropic model the check doesn't run at all, rather than guessing a limit. I said this in the comment.

